{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JEgA5Vmiti4etzumMz2jNo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Brief: Android widget foundation and read-only \"Your Day\" widget\n2\t\n3\ttype: feature\n4\tid: story\n5\tbranch: feature/story_android-widget-foundation-and-read-only-your-day-widget\n6\tdate: 2026-10-29\n7\tauthor: Leander Muskalla\n8\t\n9\t## What\n10\t\n11\tBuild the native foundation for home-screen widgets and the first widget on\n12\tit: a read-only \"Your Day\" list (today's events, due and overdue todos,\n13\tupcoming events). Tapping a row opens the matching page in the app. Tap-to-\n14\tcomplete comes in [[android-widget-tap-to-complete]], on this foundation.\n15\t\n16\tThis is job 5 of 6 in `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets-decisions.md`\n17\t(D3, D6, D7, D9, D11, D12). Read that document first. It depends on the API\n18\tjobs (`widget-token`, `widget-your-day-and-complete-action` in\n19\t`solyto/api`) and the app job (`android-widget-bridge` in `solyto/app`).\n20\t\n21\t## Why\n22\t\n23\tUsers want their day at a glance without opening the app. Every later widget\n24\treuses what this job builds: the bridge, the token store, fetching, the list\n25\trenderer, routing and the error states.\n26\t\n27\t## Contract with the API and the app\n28\t\n29\tThe API and app jobs live in other repos and are not visible from here. This\n30\tsection is the complete contract this job relies on. Build against it\n31\texactly; do not guess anything beyond it.\n32\t\n33\t### Bridge messages (`../app`, vendored into `frontend/`)\n34\t\n35\tThe app looks for `window.SolytoWidgets` (from `addWebMessageListener`).\n36\tMessages are JSON strings. The app sends with `SolytoWidgets.postMessage(...)`;\n37\tnative replies and native-initiated messages go through the `JsReplyProxy`\n38\tand arrive in the app on `SolytoWidgets.onmessage`.\n39\t\n40\tApp → native:\n41\t\n42\t| Message | When |\n43\t|---|---|\n44\t| `{ \"type\": \"ready\" }` | Once per app start, after auth has loaded and the router is ready |\n45\t| `{ \"type\": \"setToken\", \"token\": \"…\", \"expiresAt\": \"<ISO 8601>\", \"apiUrl\": \"https://…\" }` | After the app issued a widget token (after `status` with `needsToken: true`, after login, after every app token refresh) |\n46\t| `{ \"type\": \"clear\" }` | On any logout, before the app clears its own state |\n47\t| `{ \"type\": \"refresh\" }` | After todo or calendar data changed (already debounced by the app) |\n48\t\n49\tNative → app:\n50\t\n51\t| Message | Meaning |\n52\t|---|---|\n53\t| `{ \"type\": \"status\", \"needsToken\": true \\| false }` | Reply to `ready`. `true` when native has no token or the stored one has expired |\n54\t| `{ \"type\": \"navigate\", \"key\": \"…\", \"id\": \"…\" }` | A widget row tap. `id` is optional. Keys used now: `todo` (with a todo UUID) and `calendar` (no id). The app maps keys to pages and ignores unknown ones |\n55\t\n56\tThe widget token is never sent back to the app.\n57\t\n58\t### API: `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/your-day`\n59\t\n60\t`apiUrl` is the value from `setToken`: the bare server URL the user\n61\tconfigured, without a path and without a trailing slash (for example\n62\t`https://api.solyto.app`, or a self-hosted server's URL). Native appends the\n63\tAPI path itself: `/api/v1/widgets/...`. This matches the app, whose API base is\n64\t`${apiUrl}/api/v1`. Request headers:\n65\t`Authorization: Bearer <widget token>`, `Accept: application/json`,\n66\t`X-Client-Version: <app version>`.\n67\t\n68\tSuccess: 200, inside the standard envelope\n69\t`{ \"success\": true, \"message\": \"…\", \"data\": { … }, \"timestamp\": \"…\" }`.\n70\t`data`:\n71\t\n72\t```\n73\t{\n74\t  \"kind\": \"your-day\",\n75\t  \"schema_version\": 1,\n76\t  \"generated_at\": \"<ISO 8601>\",\n77\t  \"refresh_at\": \"<ISO 8601 with offset>\",    // next local midnight in the user's timezone\n78\t  \"labels\": { \"title\": \"…\", \"empty\": \"…\" },  // translated\n79\t  \"sections\": [{\n80\t    \"key\": \"today\" | \"due\" | \"upcoming\",\n81\t    \"title\": \"…\",                            // translated\n82\t    \"rows\": [{\n83\t      \"id\": \"…\",\n84\t      \"title\": \"…\",\n85\t      \"subtitle\": \"…\",                       // optional, e.g. \"Overdue · 27 Oct\"\n86\t      \"time_label\": \"…\",                     // optional, e.g. \"14:00 – 15:00\", \"All day\"\n87\t      \"at\": \"…\", \"until\": \"…\",               // optional; ISO timestamps, or Y-m-d dates when all_day\n88\t      \"all_day\": true | false,\n89\t      \"icon\": \"event\" | \"todo\",              // optional\n90\t      \"route\": { \"key\": \"todo\" | \"calendar\", \"id\": \"…\" },   // id only for todo\n91\t      \"action\": { \"type\": \"check\", \"key\": \"todo.complete\", \"checked\": false }  // optional, todo rows\n92\t    }]\n93\t  }]\n94\t}\n95\t```\n96\t\n97\t- All display text is ready to show (user's language, timezone, time and\n98\t  date format). Native formats nothing.\n99\t- Empty sections are left out; no sections at all means show `labels.empty`.\n100\t  At most 20 rows per section.\n101\t- Additive changes keep `schema_version` 1: ignore unknown fields, section\n102\t  keys, icons and action types. A `schema_version` above 1 means \"update the\n103\t  app\".\n104\t- `action` is rendered only in [[android-widget-tap-to-complete]]; this job\n105\t  ignores it.\n106\t\n107\t### API status codes\n108\t\n109\t| Status | Meaning | Native does |\n110\t|---|---|---|\n111\t| 200 | Data | Render, cache, schedule `refresh_at` |\n112\t| 401 | Widget token invalid or expired (also after logout or session revocation) | Delete the local token, show \"Open solyto to sign in\" |\n113\t| 404 | The server has no widget routes (old self-hosted server) | Show \"Your server doesn't support widgets yet\" |\n114\t| 426 | App below the server's minimum version | Show \"Please update the app\" |\n115\t| 429 | Rate-limited | Keep the last data, mark it as outdated, back off |\n116\t| 5xx / no response | Server or network problem | Same as 429 |\n117\t\n118\t## Steps\n119\t\n120\t1. **Already vendored:** `frontend/` already contains the app with the widget\n121\t   bridge (`frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts`) and the Italian\n122\t   translation. Do **not** run `scripts/vendor.sh` (`../app` is not available\n123\t   here). Just confirm the file exists; it is the JS side of the contract\n124\t   above.\n125\t2. **Bridge:** a Capacitor plugin (registered in `MainActivity` like\n126\t   `PullToRefreshPlugin`, so it is set up before the first page loads) that\n127\t   calls `WebViewCompat.addWebMessageListener` with the name `SolytoWidgets`\n128\t   and the allowed origin from `getBridge().getLocalUrl()`\n129\t   (`https://my.solyto.app`).\n130\t   - Accept main-frame messages only; ignore anything malformed.\n131\t   - Implement the contract from the app job exactly: `ready` → reply\n132\t     `{type:\"status\", needsToken}` and deliver a pending route; `setToken`;\n133\t     `clear`; `refresh`. Native → app: `{type:\"navigate\", key, id?}` through\n134\t     the reply proxy kept from `ready`.\n135\t   - If `WEB_MESSAGE_LISTENER` is not supported, register nothing; widgets\n136\t     show a \"not supported on this device\" state.\n137\t   - Never return the token to JS.\n138\t3. **Token store:** an AES-GCM key in the AndroidKeyStore encrypts the\n139\t   token; the ciphertext, IV, expiry and API URL go into private\n140\t   `SharedPreferences`. `needsToken` is true when there is no token or it has\n141\t   expired. `clear` deletes the token and the cached widget data. Do not use\n142\t   `androidx.security:security-crypto` (deprecated).\n143\t4. **Backup exclusion:** exclude the token prefs and the widget data cache\n144\t   (`android:fullBackupContent` for API ≤ 30, `android:dataExtractionRules`\n145\t   for API 31+). Manifest change: flag it in review.\n146\t5. **Fetching:** `HttpURLConnection` + `org.json`, `Authorization: Bearer`\n147\t   with the widget token, `X-Client-Version` with the app version. The token\n148\t   and full responses are never logged.\n149\t6. **Workers** (`androidx.work:work-runtime`):\n150\t   - a periodic fetch every 60 minutes, scheduled in the provider's\n151\t     `onEnabled`, cancelled in `onDisabled`;\n152\t   - a one-off fetch at the payload's `refresh_at`;\n153\t   - a one-off fetch on `refresh`, `setToken` and when a widget is added;\n154\t   - the token is **never** put into WorkManager input data; workers read it\n155\t     from the token store;\n156\t   - `updatePeriodMillis=\"0\"` in the provider XML.\n157\t7. **Your Day widget** (`AppWidgetProvider` + `RemoteViews`, list via\n158\t   `androidx.core:core-remoteviews` `RemoteCollectionItems`):\n159\t   - renders the generic format: section headers, rows with `title`,\n160\t     `subtitle`, `time_label`, icon from a fixed set (`event`, `todo`);\n161\t     unknown section, row or icon types are skipped, not errors; a higher\n162\t     `schema_version` than supported shows the \"update the app\" state;\n163\t   - `labels.empty` when there are no sections;\n164\t   - a header with the title and \"updated at\"; tapping it opens the app;\n165\t   - light and dark (`values-night`), using the existing colour resources;\n166\t   - `appwidget-provider` XML with a preview image and description, sensible\n167\t     default and minimum sizes, resizable.\n168\t8. **Routing (D6):** rows use the mutable template `PendingIntent` (explicit\n169\t   `MainActivity` component) plus per-row fill-in intents carrying\n170\t   `route.key` and `route.id`. `MainActivity` handles them in `onCreate` and\n171\t   `onNewIntent`: validate the key format (`[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*`) and the id\n172\t   length, then send `navigate` if the app is ready, or keep it until\n173\t   `ready` arrives. Native keeps no list of paths; the app maps keys.\n174\t   Other widget `PendingIntent`s are explicit and `FLAG_IMMUTABLE`, with\n175\t   distinct request codes.\n176\t9. **States (D11):** loading; signed out (\"Open solyto to sign in\", on 401:\n177\t   delete the local token too); server without widgets (404 on the widget\n178\t   route, D12); \"Please update the app\" (426 or unknown `schema_version`);\n179\t   offline/429/5xx: keep the last data, mark it as outdated, back off; not\n180\t   supported on this device.\n181\t10. **Strings** in `values` and `values-de/fr/es/it`: picker name and\n182\t    description and all states. Content text comes from the server.\n183\t11. **Dependencies:** only `androidx.core:core-remoteviews` and\n184\t    `androidx.work:work-runtime` are new (Apache-2.0, Google Maven, no GMS).\n185\t    Add versions to `variables.gradle` like the others. Confirm the F-Droid\n186\t    build (`fdroid/`) needs no change.\n187\t12. **Manual checks** (report §7.6): place, resize and remove the widget;\n188\t    light/dark; API 24 and API 34+ emulators; login → data appears; logout →\n189\t    signed-out state; app token refresh → widget keeps working; tap a todo\n190\t    row and an event row, both warm and cold start; airplane mode; server\n191\t    URL of an old self-hosted server; reboot.\n192\t\n193\t## Out of scope\n194\t\n195\t- Tap-to-complete ([[android-widget-tap-to-complete]]).\n196\t- Other widgets, static app shortcuts, a widget setup screen.\n197\t- Moving the share intent to the bridge.\n198\t\n199\t## Notes\n200\t\n201\t- `MainActivity` is exported; a forged intent can at most open a known page.\n202\t- Native uses exactly the API URL from `setToken`, under the same network\n203\t  security rules as the WebView.\n204\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e8c61e8-895f-4f65-b097-20b0f80cb23c","uuid":"ea255575-d5e3-4e10-86a0-b84201e098a3","timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:42:38.174Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/story_android-widget-foundation-and-read-only-your-day-widget/brief.md","content":"# Brief: Android widget foundation and read-only \"Your Day\" widget\n\ntype: feature\nid: story\nbranch: feature/story_android-widget-foundation-and-read-only-your-day-widget\ndate: 2026-10-29\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nBuild the native foundation for home-screen widgets and the first widget on\nit: a read-only \"Your Day\" list (today's events, due and overdue todos,\nupcoming events). Tapping a row opens the matching page in the app. Tap-to-\ncomplete comes in [[android-widget-tap-to-complete]], on this foundation.\n\nThis is job 5 of 6 in `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets-decisions.md`\n(D3, D6, D7, D9, D11, D12). Read that document first. It depends on the API\njobs (`widget-token`, `widget-your-day-and-complete-action` in\n`solyto/api`) and the app job (`android-widget-bridge` in `solyto/app`).\n\n## Why\n\nUsers want their day at a glance without opening the app. Every later widget\nreuses what this job builds: the bridge, the token store, fetching, the list\nrenderer, routing and the error states.\n\n## Contract with the API and the app\n\nThe API and app jobs live in other repos and are not visible from here. This\nsection is the complete contract this job relies on. Build against it\nexactly; do not guess anything beyond it.\n\n### Bridge messages (`../app`, vendored into `frontend/`)\n\nThe app looks for `window.SolytoWidgets` (from `addWebMessageListener`).\nMessages are JSON strings. The app sends with `SolytoWidgets.postMessage(...)`;\nnative replies and native-initiated messages go through the `JsReplyProxy`\nand arrive in the app on `SolytoWidgets.onmessage`.\n\nApp → native:\n\n| Message | When |\n|---|---|\n| `{ \"type\": \"ready\" }` | Once per app start, after auth has loaded and the router is ready |\n| `{ \"type\": \"setToken\", \"token\": \"…\", \"expiresAt\": \"<ISO 8601>\", \"apiUrl\": \"https://…\" }` | After the app issued a widget token (after `status` with `needsToken: true`, after login, after every app token refresh) |\n| `{ \"type\": \"clear\" }` | On any logout, before the app clears its own state |\n| `{ \"type\": \"refresh\" }` | After todo or calendar data changed (already debounced by the app) |\n\nNative → app:\n\n| Message | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `{ \"type\": \"status\", \"needsToken\": true \\| false }` | Reply to `ready`. `true` when native has no token or the stored one has expired |\n| `{ \"type\": \"navigate\", \"key\": \"…\", \"id\": \"…\" }` | A widget row tap. `id` is optional. Keys used now: `todo` (with a todo UUID) and `calendar` (no id). The app maps keys to pages and ignores unknown ones |\n\nThe widget token is never sent back to the app.\n\n### API: `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/your-day`\n\n`apiUrl` is the value from `setToken`: the bare server URL the user\nconfigured, without a path and without a trailing slash (for example\n`https://api.solyto.app`, or a self-hosted server's URL). Native appends the\nAPI path itself: `/api/v1/widgets/...`. This matches the app, whose API base is\n`${apiUrl}/api/v1`. Request headers:\n`Authorization: Bearer <widget token>`, `Accept: application/json`,\n`X-Client-Version: <app version>`.\n\nSuccess: 200, inside the standard envelope\n`{ \"success\": true, \"message\": \"…\", \"data\": { … }, \"timestamp\": \"…\" }`.\n`data`:\n\n```\n{\n  \"kind\": \"your-day\",\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"generated_at\": \"<ISO 8601>\",\n  \"refresh_at\": \"<ISO 8601 with offset>\",    // next local midnight in the user's timezone\n  \"labels\": { \"title\": \"…\", \"empty\": \"…\" },  // translated\n  \"sections\": [{\n    \"key\": \"today\" | \"due\" | \"upcoming\",\n    \"title\": \"…\",                            // translated\n    \"rows\": [{\n      \"id\": \"…\",\n      \"title\": \"…\",\n      \"subtitle\": \"…\",                       // optional, e.g. \"Overdue · 27 Oct\"\n      \"time_label\": \"…\",                     // optional, e.g. \"14:00 – 15:00\", \"All day\"\n      \"at\": \"…\", \"until\": \"…\",               // optional; ISO timestamps, or Y-m-d dates when all_day\n      \"all_day\": true | false,\n      \"icon\": \"event\" | \"todo\",              // optional\n      \"route\": { \"key\": \"todo\" | \"calendar\", \"id\": \"…\" },   // id only for todo\n      \"action\": { \"type\": \"check\", \"key\": \"todo.complete\", \"checked\": false }  // optional, todo rows\n    }]\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n- All display text is ready to show (user's language, timezone, time and\n  date format). Native formats nothing.\n- Empty sections are left out; no sections at all means show `labels.empty`.\n  At most 20 rows per section.\n- Additive changes keep `schema_version` 1: ignore unknown fields, section\n  keys, icons and action types. A `schema_version` above 1 means \"update the\n  app\".\n- `action` is rendered only in [[android-widget-tap-to-complete]]; this job\n  ignores it.\n\n### API status codes\n\n| Status | Meaning | Native does |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 | Data | Render, cache, schedule `refresh_at` |\n| 401 | Widget token invalid or expired (also after logout or session revocation) | Delete the local token, show \"Open solyto to sign in\" |\n| 404 | The server has no widget routes (old self-hosted server) | Show \"Your server doesn't support widgets yet\" |\n| 426 | App below the server's minimum version | Show \"Please update the app\" |\n| 429 | Rate-limited | Keep the last data, mark it as outdated, back off |\n| 5xx / no response | Server or network problem | Same as 429 |\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Already vendored:** `frontend/` already contains the app with the widget\n   bridge (`frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts`) and the Italian\n   translation. Do **not** run `scripts/vendor.sh` (`../app` is not available\n   here). Just confirm the file exists; it is the JS side of the contract\n   above.\n2. **Bridge:** a Capacitor plugin (registered in `MainActivity` like\n   `PullToRefreshPlugin`, so it is set up before the first page loads) that\n   calls `WebViewCompat.addWebMessageListener` with the name `SolytoWidgets`\n   and the allowed origin from `getBridge().getLocalUrl()`\n   (`https://my.solyto.app`).\n   - Accept main-frame messages only; ignore anything malformed.\n   - Implement the contract from the app job exactly: `ready` → reply\n     `{type:\"status\", needsToken}` and deliver a pending route; `setToken`;\n     `clear`; `refresh`. Native → app: `{type:\"navigate\", key, id?}` through\n     the reply proxy kept from `ready`.\n   - If `WEB_MESSAGE_LISTENER` is not supported, register nothing; widgets\n     show a \"not supported on this device\" state.\n   - Never return the token to JS.\n3. **Token store:** an AES-GCM key in the AndroidKeyStore encrypts the\n   token; the ciphertext, IV, expiry and API URL go into private\n   `SharedPreferences`. `needsToken` is true when there is no token or it has\n   expired. `clear` deletes the token and the cached widget data. Do not use\n   `androidx.security:security-crypto` (deprecated).\n4. **Backup exclusion:** exclude the token prefs and the widget data cache\n   (`android:fullBackupContent` for API ≤ 30, `android:dataExtractionRules`\n   for API 31+). Manifest change: flag it in review.\n5. **Fetching:** `HttpURLConnection` + `org.json`, `Authorization: Bearer`\n   with the widget token, `X-Client-Version` with the app version. The token\n   and full responses are never logged.\n6. **Workers** (`androidx.work:work-runtime`):\n   - a periodic fetch every 60 minutes, scheduled in the provider's\n     `onEnabled`, cancelled in `onDisabled`;\n   - a one-off fetch at the payload's `refresh_at`;\n   - a one-off fetch on `refresh`, `setToken` and when a widget is added;\n   - the token is **never** put into WorkManager input data; workers read it\n     from the token store;\n   - `updatePeriodMillis=\"0\"` in the provider XML.\n7. **Your Day widget** (`AppWidgetProvider` + `RemoteViews`, list via\n   `androidx.core:core-remoteviews` `RemoteCollectionItems`):\n   - renders the generic format: section headers, rows with `title`,\n     `subtitle`, `time_label`, icon from a fixed set (`event`, `todo`);\n     unknown section, row or icon types are skipped, not errors; a higher\n     `schema_version` than supported shows the \"update the app\" state;\n   - `labels.empty` when there are no sections;\n   - a header with the title and \"updated at\"; tapping it opens the app;\n   - light and dark (`values-night`), using the existing colour resources;\n   - `appwidget-provider` XML with a preview image and description, sensible\n     default and minimum sizes, resizable.\n8. **Routing (D6):** rows use the mutable template `PendingIntent` (explicit\n   `MainActivity` component) plus per-row fill-in intents carrying\n   `route.key` and `route.id`. `MainActivity` handles them in `onCreate` and\n   `onNewIntent`: validate the key format (`[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*`) and the id\n   length, then send `navigate` if the app is ready, or keep it until\n   `ready` arrives. Native keeps no list of paths; the app maps keys.\n   Other widget `PendingIntent`s are explicit and `FLAG_IMMUTABLE`, with\n   distinct request codes.\n9. **States (D11):** loading; signed out (\"Open solyto to sign in\", on 401:\n   delete the local token too); server without widgets (404 on the widget\n   route, D12); \"Please update the app\" (426 or unknown `schema_version`);\n   offline/429/5xx: keep the last data, mark it as outdated, back off; not\n   supported on this device.\n10. **Strings** in `values` and `values-de/fr/es/it`: picker name and\n    description and all states. Content text comes from the server.\n11. **Dependencies:** only `androidx.core:core-remoteviews` and\n    `androidx.work:work-runtime` are new (Apache-2.0, Google Maven, no GMS).\n    Add versions to `variables.gradle` like the others. Confirm the F-Droid\n    build (`fdroid/`) needs no change.\n12. **Manual checks** (report §7.6): place, resize and remove the widget;\n    light/dark; API 24 and API 34+ emulators; login → data appears; logout →\n    signed-out state; app token refresh → widget keeps working; tap a todo\n    row and an event row, both warm and cold start; airplane mode; server\n    URL of an old self-hosted server; reboot.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Tap-to-complete ([[android-widget-tap-to-complete]]).\n- Other widgets, static app shortcuts, a widget setup screen.\n- Moving the share intent to the bridge.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `MainActivity` is exported; a forged intent can at most open a known page.\n- Native uses exactly the API URL from `setToken`, under the same network\n  security rules as the WebView.\n","numLines":204,"startLine":1,"totalLines":204}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JEgA5Vmiti4etzumMz2jNo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
