 outdated marker; ListView/collection; empty and state text)","+  - row layouts (section header; item with icon, title, subtitle and time_label)","+  - `event` and `todo` vector icons","+  - `res/xml/your_day_widget_info.xml` (`updatePeriodMillis=\"0\"`, resizable, sensible min/default sizes, `previewImage` and, on API 31+, `previewLayout`, `description`)","+  - light and dark colours in `values` / `values-night`, based on the existing colour resources","+  files: android/app/src/main/res/layout/widget_your_day*.xml (new), android/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_widget_*.xml (new), android/app/src/main/res/xml/your_day_widget_info.xml (new), android/app/src/main/res/values/colors.xml, android/app/src/main/res/values-night/colors.xml (new)","+  depends: none","+  risk: medium. RemoteViews only supports a limited set of views and attributes, so an unsupported one breaks the widget at runtime, not at build time. `previewImage` needs a drawable; if no real screenshot exists, use a drawable preview and say so.","+","+TASK-9: Add strings in `values` and `values-de`, `values-fr`, `values-es` and `values-it`: widget picker name and description, loading, \"Open solyto to sign in\", \"Your server doesn't support widgets yet\", \"Please update the app\", \"Not supported on this device\", outdated marker and the \"updated at\" format.","+  files: android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml, android/app/src/main/res/values-{de,fr,es,it}/strings.xml (new)","+  depends: none","+  risk: low. Translations need a native-speaker check. The new locale folders contain only the widget strings, so `app_name` etc. fall back to the defaults.","+","+TASK-10: Create `YourDayWidgetProvider` (`AppWidgetProvider`). It:","+  - renders each state from the cache (ok list via `RemoteCollectionItems` from core-remoteviews, empty with `labels.empty`, loading, signed-out, unsupported-server, update-app, not-supported-device, with an outdated marker on stale data);","+  - in `onEnabled`, schedules periodic work and a one-off fetch; in `onDisabled`, cancels all widget work;","+  - on add/update, enqueues a one-off fetch;","+  - has an explicit `FLAG_IMMUTABLE` header PendingIntent that opens `MainActivity`;","+  - has a mutable explicit row template PendingIntent with per-row fill-in intents carrying `route.key` / `route.id`, with distinct request codes.","+  Register the provider as a receiver in the manifest.","+  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/widget/YourDayWidgetProvider.java (new), android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","+  depends: TASK-1, TASK-3, TASK-6, TASK-7, TASK-8, TASK-9","+  risk: high. This is the largest piece. Mutable vs immutable PendingIntent rules on API 31+, `RemoteCollectionItems` behaviour on API 24 vs 31+, and stable row IDs are easy to get wrong. Second manifest change; flag it.","+","+TASK-11: Create `WidgetBridgePlugin` (Capacitor plugin, registered in `MainActivity` before `super.onCreate`, like `PullToRefreshPlugin`). In `load()`, when `WebViewFeature.WEB_MESSAGE_LISTENER` is supported, it calls `WebViewCompat.addWebMessageListener(webView, \"SolytoWidgets\", {getBridge().getLocalUrl()}, …)`. If the feature is not supported, it registers nothing and records the not-supported state. It:","+  - accepts only `isMainFrame` messages that parse as JSON with a known `type`, and ignores anything malformed;","+  - on `ready`, keeps the `JsReplyProxy`, replies `{type:\"status\", needsToken}` and flushes the pending route;","+  - on `setToken`, validates and stores the token and enqueues a fetch;","+  - on `clear`, wipes the token and cache and re-renders the widgets as signed out;","+  - on `refresh`, enqueues a fetch;","+  - exposes a method to send `navigate` or keep it pending;","+  - never posts the token back.","+  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/WidgetBridgePlugin.java (new), android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/MainActivity.java","+  depends: TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-7, TASK-10 (for re-render on clear)","+  risk: high. Trust boundary. The origin rule must be exactly the local URL, `postMessage` must run on the right thread, and the reply proxy must be dropped or replaced when the page reloads (pull-to-refresh, share `loadUrl`).","+","+TASK-12: Handle widget row intents in `MainActivity` (`onCreate` + `onNewIntent`, next to `handleShareIntent`). Read the fill-in `key`/`id`, validate the key against `[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*` (bounded length) and the id length, ignore anything else, and pass the route to `WidgetBridgePlugin`. The plugin sends `navigate` now if the app is ready, or keeps it until `ready`. Native keeps no path list.","+  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/MainActivity.java, android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/WidgetBridgePlugin.java","+  depends: TASK-10, TASK-11","+  risk: medium. `MainActivity` is exported and `singleTask`, so forged intents and warm vs cold start both have to work. Use a dedicated action or extra namespace so share and launcher intents are not affected.","+","+TASK-13: Build check and handoff notes. Run `cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug` (after `make build-fdroid` or `npx cap sync android` if needed). Confirm that `fdroid/app.solyto.yml` and `scripts/build-fdroid.sh` need no change. List the manual checks from brief §12 in `implementation.md` as not yet done, and flag both manifest changes.","+  files: docs/jobs/story_android-widget-foundation-and-read-only-your-day-widget/implementation.md","+  depends: TASK-1 through TASK-12","+  risk: medium. The Gradle build may need network access for the new artifacts. If it can't run in the session, say so rather than claiming it passed. Emulator checks (API 24 and API 34+, reboot, airplane mode) can't be done in the container.","+","+## Open points (not blocking; the developer should decide and document them)","+","+- Widget preview: no design asset exists. A `previewLayout` (API 31+) plus a","+  simple drawable `previewImage` is the conservative choice.","+- Back-off for 429: the brief says \"back off\" without numbers. WorkManager's","+  exponential backoff on the one-off fetch, with the 60-minute periodic fetch","+  as the floor, needs no new constants from the API side.","+- Whether the \"not supported on this device\" state persists depends on the","+  WebView, which can be updated. Re-check it on every app start and do not","+  store it permanently."]}],"originalFile":"# Tasks: Android widget foundation and read-only \"Your Day\" widget\n\nid: story\nanalyst:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n<!-- TASK-1: description\n     files: list of files likely affected\n     depends: none\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y9Zo1rfcchvQ2jxytaFLmy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgWs5bqdffrjFqCgmcu8B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote 13 tasks to `docs/jobs/story_android-widget-foundation-and-read-only-your-day-widget/tasks.md`. Nothing needs a human decision before development can start. I couldn't run git here, so I checked the branch from the worktree's HEAD file instead: it matches the brief.\n\n**What I confirmed before planning:**\n- `frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts` exists and matches the contract in the brief, so `frontend/` needs no edits.\n- The app sends `X-Client-Version` as the root `package.json` version. That is the same value the build writes as `versionName`, so the widget should send `versionName`.\n- The app's bridge sends the bare server URL in `setToken`, and the native side adds `/api/v1/widgets/...` itself.\n\n**The tasks, roughly in order:**\n1. The two new dependencies.\n2. The encrypted token store.\n3. The widget data cache.\n4. Backup exclusion rules.\n5. The API client.\n6. The payload parser.\n7. The background fetch worker and its scheduling.\n8. Widget layouts, icons and light/dark colours.\n9. Strings in five languages.\n10. The widget itself (`YourDayWidgetProvider`).\n11. The JS ↔ native bridge plugin.\n12. Handling widget taps in `MainActivity`.\n13. A build check and handoff notes.\n\n**High risk:**\n- **Token store (TASK-2):** if the key store fails, it must treat that as \"no token\", never crash and never fall back to plain text.\n- **Widget provider (TASK-10):** the click-intent rules on Android 12+ and the list API on Android 7 vs 12+ are easy to get wrong.\n- **Bridge plugin (TASK-11):** it's a trust boundary. It must accept only the app's own origin and main frame, and handle page reloads.\n\nTASK-4 and TASK-10 both change the manifest, so they're flagged for review.\n\n**Open points the developer should decide and write down:**\n- **Preview image:** there's no design asset for the widget preview.\n- **Back-off:** the brief doesn't give numbers for backing off after 429 or server errors.\n- **\"Not supported\" state:** this one should be checked again on each app start, not stored, because the WebView can be updated.\n\nThe emulator checks from the brief's step 12 (API 24 and 34+, reboot, airplane mode) can't run in the container. They're listed as manual steps."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5375,"cache_read_input_tokens":50257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5375},"output_tokens":747,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e8c61e8-895f-4f65-b097-20b0f80cb23c","uuid":"99f828f6-f24a-46f5-8e98-00dae99ab3b6","timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:43:57.900Z","request_id":"req_011CgWs5bSLEP48xv7Vbam4m"}
