nCompileSdk 35, AGP ≥ 8.6). Both are\nfine with compileSdk 36 / AGP 8.13. `fdroid/app.solyto.yml` and\n`scripts/build-fdroid.sh` need no change: both artifacts come from Google\nMaven (allowed by F-Droid) and nothing touches the Node/frontend build.\n\nTASK-2: `widget/WidgetTokenStore.java` holds an AES-256-GCM key in\nAndroidKeyStore (`solyto_widget_token`). It writes the ciphertext, IV, expiry\nand API URL to the private prefs `widget_token`. Expiry and URL are bound in\nas GCM associated data. Any Keystore or decrypt failure clears the store and\ncounts as \"no token\", with no plaintext fallback. The token is never logged:\nonly exception class names are. `widget/IsoTime.java` parses ISO 8601 on API\n24 (java.time needs 26). `apiUrl` must be http(s) with a host and no\nquery/fragment/userinfo; trailing slashes are stripped.\n\nTASK-3: `widget/WidgetCache.java` uses the prefs `widget_cache` to hold the\nlast `data` JSON, the fetch time, an outdated flag, the state\n(LOADING/OK/SIGNED_OUT/UNSUPPORTED_SERVER/UPDATE_APP) and a\n\"device unsupported\" flag. The plugin rewrites that flag on every app start,\nso a WebView update clears it.\n\nTASK-4: adds `res/xml/backup_rules.xml` (≤ API 30) and\n`res/xml/data_extraction_rules.xml` (API 31+, cloud backup and device\ntransfer). They exclude `widget_token.xml`, `widget_cache.xml` and\n`androidx.core.widget.prefs.RemoteViewsCompat.xml` (core-remoteviews keeps\nrow content there on API < 31). **Manifest change:** `fullBackupContent` and\n`dataExtractionRules` on `<application>`.\n\nTASK-5: `widget/WidgetApi.java` calls `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/your-day`\nwith Bearer, `Accept` and `X-Client-Version` (the `versionName` from\nPackageManager, the same value as the app's `PUBLIC_VERSION`). It uses\n15 s timeouts and a 1 MB body limit, and doesn't follow redirects so the\ntoken can't leak to another host. It maps responses to OK / 401 / 404 / 426 /\ntemporary failure (429, 5xx, 3xx, other statuses, I/O, bad envelope).\n\nTASK-6: `widget/YourDayPayload.java` checks `kind: your-day` and schema\nversion 1, and flattens sections into header and row items. It skips unknown\nsection keys and rows without a title, drops unknown icons, ignores `action`,\ncaps at 20 rows per section and cuts text to 500 chars.\n\nTASK-7: `widget/WidgetFetchWorker.java` and `widget/WidgetWork.java` handle\nfetching and scheduling.\n- Unique work: a 60-minute periodic fetch (KEEP), \"now\" (REPLACE) and \"at\n  refresh_at + 1 min\" (REPLACE). Backoff is exponential from 5 minutes, with\n  at most 3 retries, after which the periodic fetch takes over.\n- No input data is passed; the worker reads the token from the store.\n- With no widget placed, `fetchNow` is a no-op. With no token, the worker\n  shows signed-out and schedules nothing.\n- If the token changed during the request (logout or a new token), the\n  result is dropped. A 401 clears the token only if it is still the one used.\n\nTASK-8: adds the layouts `widget_your_day`, `_row`, `_section` and\n`_preview`, the drawables `ic_widget_event`/`ic_widget_todo` (Lucide-style),\n`widget_background`, `widget_placeholder_bar` and `widget_preview`, and\n`res/xml/your_day_widget_info.xml`. The widget info is 180×110 dp min,\nresizable to 110×80 dp, 3×3 target cells, `updatePeriodMillis=\"0\"`, with a\ndescription, `previewImage` and `previewLayout`. Widget colours are in\n`values/colors.xml`, built on the existing solyto colours, with dark\noverrides in the new `values-night/colors.xml`.\n\nTASK-9: widget strings in `values`, plus new `values-de/fr/es/it`. The\nwording matches the web app's informal tone (du/tu/tú), and the title\nmatches the app's `your_day` translations. Needs a native-speaker check.\n\nTASK-10: `widget/YourDayWidgetProvider.java` renders from the cache with\n`RemoteCollectionItems`. The device-unsupported state takes priority, then\nthe cache state. Payload with no rows shows `labels.empty`; an unreadable\npayload shows \"update the app\". \"Updated HH:MM\" turns into \"Outdated · HH:MM\"\non stale data.\n- The header and the state text use an explicit `FLAG_IMMUTABLE`\n  PendingIntent (request code 1) that opens `MainActivity`.\n- Rows use an explicit mutable template (request code 2, action\n  `app.solyto.action.WIDGET_ROUTE`) with per-row fill-in extras.\n- `onEnabled` schedules the periodic fetch, `onDisabled` cancels all work,\n  and `onUpdate` renders and enqueues a fetch.\n- **Manifest change:** `<receiver .widget.YourDayWidgetProvider exported=\"false\">`\n  with the appwidget meta-data.\n\nTASK-11: `WidgetBridgePlugin.java` is registered in `MainActivity` before\n`super.onCreate`, like `PullToRefreshPlugin`.\n- It calls `addWebMessageListener(\"SolytoWidgets\", {getLocalUrl()})` only\n  when `WEB_MESSAGE_LISTENER` is supported; otherwise it registers nothing\n  and sets the not-supported state.\n- It accepts only main-frame string messages ≤ 16 KB that parse as JSON with\n  a known type.\n- It keeps the reply proxy from `ready` and drops it on `onPageStarted`\n  (reload, share `loadUrl`).\n- Token and cache work runs on a single-thread executor; replies go out on\n  the main thread.\n- The token is never posted back.\n\nTASK-12: `MainActivity` handles `ACTION_WIDGET_ROUTE` in `onCreate` (only on\na fresh start, not on recreation) and `onNewIntent`.\n- It ignores launches from history and consumes the extras.\n- It validates the key (`[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*`, ≤ 64) and the id (1–128 chars).\n- It hands the route to the plugin, which sends `navigate` now or keeps it\n  until `ready`.\n- Share and launcher intents are unaffected.\n\n## Flag for review\n\n- **Two manifest changes:** the backup rules attributes (TASK-4) and the\n  widget receiver (TASK-10).\n- New dependencies (TASK-1), approved by the brief §11.\n- No changes to `fdroid/`, signing, `versionCode`/`versionName`, or\n  `frontend/`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- **Build not run** (no JDK/SDK in the container). Run\n  `make build-fdroid && cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug` first.\n- **Manual checks (brief §12, none done yet):**\n  - place, resize and remove the widget\n  - light and dark mode\n  - API 24 and API 34+ emulators\n  - login → data appears\n  - logout → signed-out state\n  - app token refresh → widget keeps working\n  - tap a todo row and an event row, both on warm and cold start\n  - airplane mode\n  - server URL of an old self-hosted server\n  - reboot\n- If the very first fetch fails (offline before any data was cached), the\n  widget stays on \"Loading…\" until a later fetch succeeds. There is no\n  separate \"offline\" string in the brief's state list.\n- `previewImage` is a drawn layer-list placeholder, not a screenshot. On\n  API 31+ the `previewLayout` is used instead. A real screenshot asset could\n  replace it later.\n- Small race: a `clear` that arrives exactly between the worker's token\n  re-check and its cache write could leave one payload in the cache until\n  the next fetch, which then clears it (no token → signed out).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":19,"newStart":1,"newLines":164,"lines":[" # Implementation: Android widget foundation and read-only \"Your Day\" widget"," "," id: story","-developer:","-date:","+developer: @developer","+date: 2026-10-29"," ","-<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->","-"," ## Summary"," ","-<!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->","+Native widget foundation plus the read-only Your Day list widget, built","+against the contract in `brief.md`. It covers:"," ","+- the `SolytoWidgets` bridge (`addWebMessageListener`, app origin only, main","+  frame only)","+- a Keystore-encrypted token store and a widget data cache, both excluded","+  from backup","+- an `HttpURLConnection` API client and a WorkManager fetch worker that","+  applies the D11 error contract","+- the `RemoteViews` list widget with light/dark colours, a preview and","+  strings in en/de/fr/es/it","+- row-tap routing through `MainActivity` → bridge `navigate`","+","+`frontend/src/lib/state/WidgetBridge.ts` exists and matches the contract, so","+`frontend/` was not edited.","+","+**Not built:** the container has no JDK and no Android SDK, so","+`./gradlew assembleDebug` could not run. All the code is unverified by a","+compiler. I checked library APIs against the actual AARs (core-remoteviews","+1.1.0, work-runtime 2.11.2, webkit 1.14.0). The first step of review should","+be a local build.","+"," ## Changes"," ","-<!-- List of files changed and what changed in each. -->","+TASK-1: `android/variables.gradle` and `android/app/build.gradle` add","+`androidx.core:core-remoteviews:1.1.0` (minCompileSdk 34) and","+`androidx.work:work-runtime:2.11.2` (minCompileSdk 35, AGP ≥ 8.6). Both are","+fine with compileSdk 36 / AGP 8.13. `fdroid/app.solyto.yml` and","+`scripts/build-fdroid.sh` need no change: both artifacts come from Google","+Maven (allowed by F-Droid) and nothing touches the Node/frontend build."," ","+TASK-2: `widget/WidgetTokenStore.java` holds an AES-256-GCM key in","+AndroidKeyStore (`solyto_widget_token`). It writes the ciphertext, IV, expiry","+and API URL to the private prefs `widget_token`. Expiry and URL are bound in","+as GCM associated data. Any Keystore or decrypt failure clears the store and","+counts as \"no token\", with no plaintext fallback. The token is never logged:","+only exception class names are. `widget/IsoTime.java` parses ISO 8601 on API","+24 (java.time needs 26). `apiUrl` must be http(s) with a host and no","+query/fragment/userinfo; trailing slashes are stripped.","+","+TASK-3: `widget/WidgetCache.java` uses the prefs `widget_cache` to hold the","+last `data` JSON, the fetch time, an outdated flag, the state","+(LOADING/OK/SIGNED_OUT/UNSUPPORTED_SERVER/UPDATE_APP) and a","+\"device unsupported\" flag. The plugin rewrites that flag on every app start,","+so a WebView update clears it.","+","+TASK-4: adds `res/xml/backup_rules.xml` (≤ API 30) and","+`res/xml/data_extraction_rules.xml` (API 31+, cloud backup and device","+transfer). They exclude `widget_token.xml`, `widget_cache.xml` and","+`androidx.core.widget.prefs.RemoteViewsCompat.xml` (core-remoteviews keeps","+row content there on API < 31). **Manifest change:** `fullBackupContent` and","+`dataExtractionRules` on `<application>`.","+","+TASK-5: `widget/WidgetApi.java` calls `GET {apiUrl}/api/v1/widgets/your-day`","+with Bearer, `Accept` and `X-Client-Version` (the `versionName` from","+PackageManager, the same value as the app's `PUBLIC_VERSION`). It uses","+15 s timeouts and a 1 MB body limit, and doesn't follow redirects so the","+token can't leak to another host. It maps responses to OK / 401 / 404 / 426 /","+temporary failure (429, 5xx, 3xx, other statuses, I/O, bad envelope).","+","+TASK-6: `widget/YourDayPayload.java` checks `kind: your-day` and schema","+version 1, and flattens sections into header and row items. It skips unknown","+section keys and rows without a title, drops unknown icons, ignores `action`,","+caps at 20 rows per section and cuts text to 500 chars.","+","+TASK-7: `widget/WidgetFetchWorker.java` and `widget/WidgetWork.java` handle","+fetching and scheduling.","+- Unique work: a 60-minute periodic fetch (KEEP), \"now\" (REPLACE) and \"at","+  refresh_at + 1 min\" (REPLACE). Backoff is exponential from 5 minutes, with","+  at most 3 retries, after which the periodic fetch takes over.","+- No input data is passed; the worker reads the token from the store.","+- With no widget placed, `fetchNow` is a no-op. With no token, the worker","+  shows signed-out and schedules nothing.","+- If the token changed during the request (logout or a new token), the","+  result is dropped. A 401 clears the token only if it is still the one used.","+","+TASK-8: adds the layouts `widget_your_day`, `_row`, `_section` and","+`_preview`, the drawables `ic_widget_event`/`ic_widget_todo` (Lucide-style),","+`widget_background`, `widget_placeholder_bar` and `widget_preview`, and","+`res/xml/your_day_widget_info.xml`. The widget info is 180×110 dp min,","+resizable to 110×80 dp, 3×3 target cells, `updatePeriodMillis=\"0\"`, with a","+description, `previewImage` and `previewLayout`. Widget colours are in","+`values/colors.xml`, built on the existing solyto colours, with dark","+overrides in the new `values-night/colors.xml`.","+","+TASK-9: widget strings in `values`, plus new `values-de/fr/es/it`. The","+wording matches the web app's informal tone (du/tu/tú), and the title","+matches the app's `your_day` translations. Needs a native-speaker check.","+","+TASK-10: `widget/YourDayWidgetProvider.java` renders from the cache with","+`RemoteCollectionItems`. The device-unsupported state takes priority, then","+the cache state. Payload with no rows shows `labels.empty`; an unreadable","+payload shows \"update the app\". \"Updated HH:MM\" turns into \"Outdated · HH:MM\"","+on stale data.","+- The header and the state text use an explicit `FLAG_IMMUTABLE`","+  PendingIntent (request code 1) that opens `MainActivity`.","+- Rows use an explicit mutable template (request code 2, action","+  `app.solyto.action.WIDGET_ROUTE`) with per-row fill-in extras.","+- `onEnabled` schedules the periodic fetch, `onDisabled` cancels all work,","+  and `onUpdate` renders and enqueues a fetch.","+- **Manifest change:** `<receiver .widget.YourDayWidgetProvider exported=\"false\">`","+  with the appwidget meta-data.","+","+TASK-11: `WidgetBridgePlugin.java` is registered in `MainActivity` before","+`super.onCreate`, like `PullToRefreshPlugin`.","+- It calls `addWebMessageListener(\"SolytoWidgets\", {getLocalUrl()})` only","+  when `WEB_MESSAGE_LISTENER` is supported; otherwise it registers nothing","+  and sets the not-supported state.","+- It accepts only main-frame string messages ≤ 16 KB that parse as JSON with","+  a known type.","+- It keeps the reply proxy from `ready` and drops it on `onPageStarted`","+  (reload, share `loadUrl`).","+- Token and cache work runs on a single-thread executor; replies go out on","+  the main thread.","+- The token is never posted back.","+","+TASK-12: `MainActivity` handles `ACTION_WIDGET_ROUTE` in `onCreate` (only on","+a fresh start, not on recreation) and `onNewIntent`.","+- It ignores launches from history and consumes the extras.","+- It validates the key (`[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]*`, ≤ 64) and the id (1–128 chars).","+- It hands the route to the plugin, which sends `navigate` now or keeps it","+  until `ready`.","+- Share and launcher intents are unaffected.","+","+## Flag for review","+","+- **Two manifest changes:** the backup rules attributes (TASK-4) and the","+  widget receiver (TASK-10).","+- New dependencies (TASK-1), approved by the brief §11.","+- No changes to `fdroid/`, signing, `versionCode`/`versionName`, or","+  `frontend/`.","+"," ## Known issues / follow-ups"," ","-<!-- Anything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope but should be tracked. -->","+- **Build not run** (no JDK/SDK in the container). Run","+  `make build-fdroid && cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug` first.","+- **Manual checks (brief §12, none done yet):**","+  - place, resize and remove the widget","+  - light and dark mode","+  - API 24 and API 34+ emulators","+  - login → data appears","+  - logout → signed-out state","+  - app token refresh → widget keeps working","+  - tap a todo row and an event row, both on warm and cold start","+  - airplane mode","+  - server URL of an old self-hosted server","+  - reboot","+- If the very first fetch fails (offline before any data was cached), the","+  widget stays on \"Loading…\" until a later fetch succeeds. There is no","+  separate \"offline\" string in the brief's state list.","+- `previewImage` is a drawn layer-list placeholder, not a screenshot. On","+  API 31+ the `previewLayout` is used instead. A real screenshot asset could","+  replace it later.","+- Small race: a `clear` that arrives exactly between the worker's token","+  re-check and its cache write could leave one payload in the cache until","+  the next fetch, which then clears it (no token → signed out)."]}],"originalFile":"# Implementation: Android widget foundation and read-only \"Your Day\" widget\n\nid: story\ndeveloper:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->\n\n## Changes\n\n<!-- List of files changed and what changed in each. -->\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n<!-- Anything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope but should be tracked. -->\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0176Yj1oDoAyEqdAMhdrrReP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
