{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgWsh5gBNA5toW49AeVNE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've implemented the widget bridge and the read-only \"Your Day\" widget (all 13 tasks), but nothing has been compiled or run. The container has no JDK or Android SDK, so the first step should be `make build-fdroid && cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug`. I did check the library calls I used against the actual downloaded library files. Everything is committed and the worktree is clean.\n\n**What's in place:**\n- **Bridge:** a new plugin, registered in `MainActivity` like `PullToRefreshPlugin`, that exposes `SolytoWidgets` to the app's own page and main frame only. It handles `ready`, `setToken`, `clear` and `refresh`, and sends `status` and `navigate` back. It never sends the token back to the app.\n- **Token store:** the token is encrypted with an AES-GCM key in the AndroidKeyStore. Any key or decryption failure counts as \"no token\" rather than crashing or falling back to plain text.\n- **Fetching:** a WorkManager job fetches every 60 minutes, at `refresh_at`, and on `refresh`, `setToken` or a new widget. It handles 401, 404, 426 and 429/5xx/offline as the brief says. It never passes the token as work input and doesn't follow redirects, so the token can't reach another host.\n- **Widget:** sections and rows with `event`/`todo` icons, an empty state, a header with \"updated at\" and an \"outdated\" marker, all the error states, light and dark colours, a preview, and resizing.\n- **Strings:** English, German, French, Spanish and Italian. They follow the web app's informal tone and need a native-speaker check.\n- **Row taps:** `MainActivity` checks the route key's format and the id's length. It sends `navigate` right away if the app is ready, or holds it until `ready` arrives.\n\n**For review:**\n- **Two manifest changes:** the backup exclusion rules on `<application>`, and the new widget receiver.\n- **Backup exclusion:** besides the token and widget data files, the rules also exclude a file the remoteviews library uses to store row content on Android 11 and lower.\n- **Dependencies:** the two new ones are `core-remoteviews` 1.1.0 and `work-runtime` 2.11.2, as the brief allows. The F-Droid metadata and `build-fdroid.sh` need no change.\n- **Untouched:** `frontend/`, signing, and the version fields.\n\n**Known gaps:**\n- If the very first fetch fails, for example offline, the widget stays on \"Loading…\" until a later fetch succeeds.\n- The preview on Android 11 and lower is a drawn placeholder, not a screenshot.\n- None of the manual checks from brief §12 have been done; they're listed in `implementation.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":113113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":432},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af113cdf-2a00-442d-a3a5-a4319c5fcc06","uuid":"60133a88-1c2c-46b3-8752-3e678c9ee9fd","timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:51:59.960Z","request_id":"req_011CgWsh5LamxGvpX8kZWR84"}
